-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Army Moves
  Publisher   Imagine / Dinamic, 1987
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Army Moves (1987)(Imagine)(128K)[re-release].z80
  MD5         9c14e2564e3f9956ff6ff973dac77537

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure and all the
              scenery: the jeep, the red bridge, helicopters and jets, the
              soldier, parrots and palms. The panel in greens, its digits
              brighter than the conversion's so the points and fuel read
              easily. Figures keep a black mask edge against the scenery.
              Backdrop adds part 1's sky gradient and clouds and part 2's dark
              jungle behind the palms; it comes on with Enhanced, and the
              Backdrop off line takes it away. Text screens and the title logo
              stay as the release draws them. Source: Enhanced colours: David
              Goti (Spec256).

  Pace        original (-0.59% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              .z80 on a 128K machine, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: figures in their own colours on a double-buffered Layer 2,
              in the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap; scenery
              in its own attributes; both parts; the plot, restore and copy
              run whole at 28 MHz in pace windows; the original loading
              screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11
              safe); the game's speed restored after every hook; two tested
              cheats
              1.1: Enhanced colours as a menu option, off by default, from the
              Spec256 conversion: every figure and all the scenery on a full-
              screen Layer 2, the panel's greens with its digits brightened,
              part 1's sky gradient, clouds and part 2's dark jungle as a
              backdrop picture that comes on with Enhanced and has its own
              Backdrop off line; both fit a 1MB Next

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keys (redefine), 2 joystick, 3 play,
              4 part 2, M music on or off; part 2 asks for the access code the
              game gives at the end of part 1. The original look: figures keep
              their own colours and the scenery keeps its own; each figure's
              ink is drawn on Layer 2, in the game's own order, over the
              original bitmap. The 128K release, both parts, with its AY
              music. Fits a 1MB Next, Enhanced included. Known issues: in the
              default look part 2's small items and bullets still take the
              cell's ink, as in the original, and part 1 figures with no
              colour of their own take the sky's ink; in JNext whole runs are
              up to 1.1 percent faster than the original and the slowest
              20-update stretch is +0.05 percent. In Enhanced part 2 a new
              room takes 40 to 55 percent longer, up to 20 frames, so its
              slowest stretch reads +11 to +20 percent and its busy scenes up
              to +2.5 percent. An occasional interrupt can be lost while the
              game's own sound code has interrupts off. Missing: natural play
              to the end; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  The archive's POKEs for this 128K release, part 1, each tested alone in the
  simulator, same keys with and without it: Infinite lives (lives never fall),
  Immunity (lives never fall). Left out: Jeep doesn't fall and No enemies (no
  clear result in testing).

